# Unit-complex phases and genuine native collar smoothness

The actual collar-adjusted cusp gamma map gives an ambient continuous
unit-complex phase, invariant under the original delta action.  The
original punctured phase is real smooth through its actual logarithmic
cover and inverse period coordinates.  Exact outer-collar agreement then
proves smoothness of the full-cap phase on an actual neighborhood of the
closed relative collar, in both original native and common cusp atlases.

No additive-circle atlas, global smoothness of the pasted core, or
submersion statement is introduced by this package.
